# IoT-IDS environment configuration — copy to `.env` and edit.
#   cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is gitignored (never commit real values). These are all OPTIONAL;
# sensible defaults apply when unset. Nothing here contains a secret.

# ── Datasets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the SFAF/cross-dataset loaders look for the datasets. Defaults to the
# repo's ./Datasets (which may be a symlink to an external drive). Point this at
# your drive if you don't want to use the symlink.
# IOTIDS_DATASETS_ROOT=/Volumes/GOAT/College/Btech_Project/Datasets

# ── Live sensor (src/ids_daemon.py) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Network interface to sniff on the Pi (eth0 = wired, wlan0 = Wi-Fi).
# IOTIDS_IFACE=eth0
# Minimum confidence for the IPS to actively block a source (0-1).
# IOTIDS_IPS_MIN_CONF=0.9
# How long an IPS block lasts, seconds.
# IOTIDS_BLOCK_SECONDS=300

# ── Dashboard (src/dashboard.py) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# IOTIDS_DASHBOARD_PORT=8080

# ── Kaggle (dataset downloads) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Kaggle API token is NOT stored here. Place it at ~/.kaggle/kaggle.json
# (chmod 600) — see code/download_datasets.py. Create one at
# https://www.kaggle.com/settings -> "Create New Token".
